{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"As of November 6, 2026, [Rule 6c-11](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-270.6c-11) requires prominent disclosure on a **free, publicly accessible website**:\n\n- **Before regular trading opens:** portfolio holdings underlying the next NAV calculation, including ticker (if applicable), CUSIP/other identifier, description, quantity and portfolio weight.\n- **Daily:** prior-business-day NAV/share, market price and premium/discount.\n- **History:** premium/discount day-count table and daily premium/discount line graph covering the latest completed calendar year and completed quarters since then—or available history for younger ETFs.\n- **Spread:** median bid–ask spread over the latest 30 calendar days, calculated using the rule’s prescribed NBBO methodology.\n- **Sustained deviation:** if a premium or discount exceeds 2% for more than seven consecutive trading days, disclose that fact and discuss factors reasonably believed materially responsible; retain both disclosures for at least one year.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Portfolio holdings are not creation/redemption transaction baskets; the rule does not require public basket disclosure."}}
